      "value": "@{6026b24dad4389164dbfa27e|full_name}: not want to get into detail but the vrcw files (currently not available to dl yet on the site in question) wouldnt differ from those the api currently still spits out, with the - in theory - (at least partial, splitted) monobehaviours included.\nI downloaded a vrca file from their site of one of my private avatar ids and it didnt differ from the unitypackage from the api. note that they only offer the latest windows package, so one wouldnt have to worry about their android (where ripping and modding arent problems just yet) avatars and prob worlds at this point (although im sure they just store everything they can, android or windows, and every version, just like this emvrc shit does).\nBut i think on emvrc you could in theory request that your data would get deleted, but couldnt confirm this yet, didnt get a mail reply.\nSame goes for https://en.vrcw.net, glad they only store the metadata here.\nAnother problem with the said site is they even make money distributing our creations (you have to buy \"privatate\" packages (set to private at the crawl time)).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
