      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Realistically there's no real way to completely stop rippers.\n\nIf you wanted to 100% stop rippers you would need to make VRChat an entirely cloud based application that streams the game to you (Imagine the now dead Google Stadia), which trust me, nobody wants.\n\nEven really trying to \"encrypt\" avatar files wouldn't be full proof either, as those encryptions can still be broken into, and it would still be possible to rip using other methods.\n\nGenerally it would end up being a never ending game of cat and mouse of constantly trying to change the encryption and wasting development time that could be spent on other features.\n\nTrust me, as an avatar creator myself it can suck, but it shouldn't be something you beat yourself up over.\n\nGenerally if you want to avoid avatar piracy I highly recommend to make the avatars you provide accessible and easy to get, especially don't add any \"DRM\" nonsense, that kind of stuff is not only a grey area in TOS, but would easily be removed by piraters and only inconvenience buyers.\n\nI could go into it a bit more but I'm short on time and need to get some stuff done.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
